<title>LEBANON: Lebanon's trade deficit $426 mln in Jan.</title>
<headline>Lebanon's trade deficit $426 mln in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon had a $426 million trade deficit in January compared with $493 million in January 1996, according to customs figures released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The customs issued the following trade details (in millions of dollars):</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE     Jan 97	   Jan 96	   Jan 95</p>
<p>    Exports		    89		 78		 51</p>
<p>    Imports		   515		571		593</p>
<p>    Trade balance	  -426	     -493	     -542</p>
<p>CUSTOMS REVENUES (in billions of Lebanese pounds)</p>
<p>				  124		126		 70</p>
<p>($1= 1,549.75 Lebanese pounds end of January 1997)</p>
<p>($1= 1,591.5 Lebanese pounds end of January 1996)</p>
<p>($1= 1,643 Lebanese pounds end of January 1995)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 745307 745308 602057</p>
